{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/913570-hints-warnings-and-insta-kill-powers-can-the-latter-be-used-on-pcs","id":913570,"title":"Hints, warnings and Insta kill powers. Can the latter be used on PCs??","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-13T12:13:25-07:00","id":913570,"title":"Hints, warnings and Insta kill powers. Can the latter be used on PCs??","content":"On most every gaming related site i go to, i ask a question in the realms of<br /> When do you (as a gm) feel that giving hints/warnings are appropriate.<br /> <br /> Do you feel that a gm is required/obligated to give them?<br /> <br /> How many do YOU give? How many do you think is required?<br /> <br /> Do you feel that a gm should be required to start the 'ball rolling' by dropping a hint, for the players to pick up on and go into?<br /> <br /> Do you feel that it is the GMs responsibility to warn them/give them hints, when something bad is going to happen to them? What about if they have done nothing to 'get that hint; like say they have an underworld contract out on them. If they have not checked with any of their underworld friends, then, realistically how would they get any warning/hint?<br /> <br /> How many hints do you give before you actually have the 'bad thing' come about?<br /> <br /> Do you still spring the 'bad thing' even if they have not picked up on those hints/warnings???<br /> <br /> As an example of why i am wondering this, I present the following (note the stats for the NPC\u2019s mentioned are using the Star wars D6 game).<br /> <br /> Back in 94-95, during a 14th month long star wars game, the players (6 total, which increased to 7 during the latter 8 months), were having 'fun' harassing a major Hutt. After every time that they messed with his plans (like hijacking a shipment of arms, spice etc) he sent a response. This started off with just gooks. Then went to thugs, major thugs and so on.<br /> <br /> Players have foiled yet another plan of the resident Hutt, and even got to his inner sanctum and had him in a standoff. 2 Pcs with grenade belts standing next to him, while 3 of his guards had TD's on the other pcs. One went, they would all go. Rather than do that, they decided to leave. This humiliation IMO was the last straw for the Hutt. He tapped into his personal funds, and contracted out 2 well known and outstanding snipers to take out the 4 main players in the party (main players, the ones who plotted and overcame his machinations).<br /> <br /> One <b>sniper</b>, had like 9d in sneak, and 11d in firearms. The other was 8d/10d, and both had silenced rifles. First time they struck, it was after the players settled into a routine for almost a month on their home planet. I had both snipers roll investigations and kept track of their rolls, when they were made etc. Had 1 strike, player #2, while the other struck player #7 (2 of the 4 main ones). When they both went down, the game stopped due to the players thinking i was trying to f**k them over. WE spent over 4 hours arguing about it, and even with me explaining, showing them the notes, they still felt that a GM should never have the bad guys do things like that....<br /> <br /> None of the players for the last 2 sessions, which i had building up to this encounter, even checked with ANY of their underworld contacts. And from prior experience, even if they had got a warning from their contacts, they would have not acted on it (as they saw it as a badge of honor).<br /> <br /> So looking at that, and to the questions above..<br /> 1) Did I do right, by having the assassin/snipers strike without warning them?<br /> 2) did I not give enough hinting?<br /> 3) should I have pushed hints onto them even though they did nothing to warrant IMO getting any?<br /> 4) Should I have held off having the snipers strike until AFTER they had bothered to check, and therefore possibly get a warning that they had a hint out on them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T12:49:50-07:00","id":913598,"title":"","content":"Table Top RP lives and dies on the trust between players and GM. Much of that trust hinges on the idea that, no matter how bleak things get, the GM has the players enjoyment in mind. <br /> <br /> Being sniped by adversaries you don't see coming (and have no reason to suspect) is fucking awful. It doesn't matter that those snipers had good rolls, it doesn't matter that they were hired by a known NPC who the players had crossed, all that matters is that from the players POV you randomly killed two of them. Robbing them of those characters, truncating the stories and making them fearful that other unseen threats could bonk them whenever you please.<br /> <br /> This was one of those moments when the storyteller has to look at the field, ignoring all rolls, and ask &quot;Is this going to be fun/exciting&quot; if the answer is no, something must be done. Personally, I'd have curtailed the first sniper's damage, have them deal a devastating blow, but not fatal, and give them player a life or death scene where they have to escape an unseen shooter. Second shooter would need a different scene, possibly later when several players can get in on the action, capture him, and suss out who hired him. That would have been a story, and a feather in the cap of the survivor. <br /> <br /> TL;DR: Killing characters with unseen forces is the #1 way to lose the trust of your players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T13:08:59-07:00","id":913616,"title":"","content":"Its one of those things that's very difficult to gauge on one hand players are expected to help the story move, on the other at some point their actions have to have consequences. <br /> <br /> Personally I have a sort of house rule I call &quot;Are you sure&quot;, basically it works like this: When a new player joins the table I explain this to them, If I ever stop the game and pointedly look at them and say in an even, calm, but forceful tone, &quot;Are you sure you want to do that?&quot; I'm giving the player the warning that what they are going to do is incredibly foolish and dangerous and I will not be responsible for what happens to their character; there will be no fudged dice, no last minute NPC rescue squads, no deus ex machina, and no mercy. I have never had to use this, but its there for when someone has a blatantly suicidal plan (that's not mentioned in jest) which the only outcome I can see is their death; generally this is for things like if the newly embraced Brujah decides he's going to beat the hell out of the Prince in the middle of Elysium. The hope is that if I ever have to use this the player will rethink their decision and choose a less immediately fatal course of action and if it doesn't I have a clear conscience over the result regardless of what happens.<br /> <br /> Your specific example is something different as I would not have invoked that rule since their actions with the hutt weren't as blatantly suicidal or stupid as what I'm suggesting the rule for. Really the only thing I would say is you should have probably had one of their contacts drop a hint something was wrong maybe a day or two before your snipers were gonna make the hit; something like, &quot;We've done good business in the past and as I was going through some 'financial records' I noticed that hutt you dealt with a month back just shifted some massive cred, he's up to something in your backyard.&quot; If your players ignored the hint and didn't even start looking into it, then by all means actions have consequences and in future games the story of what happened to those characters is now a cautionary tale of why you don't cross that hutt. The reason I say that is because unless I'm missing something or you skipped over something, to the players it looks like a month of relative down time then the character is dead from a bullet to the brain. You said you kept track of dice rolls and such for the snipers, but if they basically all succeeded the players had no idea what was going on (and just assuming the ST is up to something because they are rolling dice should not be the only hint as that is purely out of game knowledge). As an outsider looking in here is what I think might have gone through your player's heads, &quot;The ST is pissed we messed up his hutt NPC so he made these godlike snipers to hunt us down, and because he didn't &quot;fail&quot; his rolls [which I'm assuming weren't rolled with the players knowledge] we get shot with no chance to defend ourselves; might have just as well said rocks fall everyone dies.&quot; Basically it looks like you took unilateral revenge against the characters through ST fiat (again assuming rolls weren't made in front if the players) since it seems like all you have validating your actions to them are notes that boil down to you die because I said so and wrote that on these sheets of paper. Also as far as I can tell the players were never prompted to roll dice on their own behalf throughout this tracking and hunting process (I'm not experienced with the system if I'm missing something mechanically please let me know), which is usually a big no-no since it removes all sense of agency from the players regarding their characters, and even being told to roll dice is not enough of a hint that something is wrong since that still relies on an out of game hint.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01","name":"Cynic01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T23:29:04-07:00","id":913904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/913570-hints-warnings-and-insta-kill-powers-can-the-latter-be-used-on-pcs?p=913598#post913598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Table Top RP lives and dies on the trust between players and GM. Much of that trust hinges on the idea that, no matter how bleak things get, the GM has the players enjoyment in mind.<br /> <br /> Being sniped by adversaries you don't see coming (and have no reason to suspect) is fucking awful. It doesn't matter that those snipers had good rolls, it doesn't matter that they were hired by a known NPC who the players had crossed, all that matters is that from the players POV you randomly killed two of them. Robbing them of those characters, truncating the stories and making them fearful that other unseen threats could bonk them whenever you please.<br /> <br /> This was one of those moments when the storyteller has to look at the field, ignoring all rolls, and ask &quot;Is this going to be fun/exciting&quot; if the answer is no, something must be done. Personally, I'd have curtailed the first sniper's damage, have them deal a devastating blow, but not fatal, and give them player a life or death scene where they have to escape an unseen shooter. Second shooter would need a different scene, possibly later when several players can get in on the action, capture him, and suss out who hired him. That would have been a story, and a feather in the cap of the survivor.<br /> <br /> TL;DR: Killing characters with unseen forces is the #1 way to lose the trust of your players.</div> </div> </div> </div>So even after all sorts of hints, warnings and such were given, just cause it 'squishes fun' don't have it go off, or neuter it?<br /> <br /> As a related q.. Say in game someone has a Maneuver that if used can do X minimum damage, which to a normal &quot;healthy&quot; person would put them CLOSE to death (ie for vampire, it takes them down to the <i>Crippled, -5d</i> level, but the baddie who has that maneuver is in combat with someone who's already down to say <i>wounded, -2d</i> level, so if its USED the minmum damage would kill said pc..<br /> Do you have him use said maneuver? If not, why not??<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cynic01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/913570-hints-warnings-and-insta-kill-powers-can-the-latter-be-used-on-pcs?p=913616#post913616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its one of those things that's very difficult to gauge on one hand players are expected to help the story move, on the other at some point their actions have to have consequences.</div> </div> </div> </div>its one of the reasons i like asking this question..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cynic01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/913570-hints-warnings-and-insta-kill-powers-can-the-latter-be-used-on-pcs?p=913616#post913616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your specific example is something different as I would not have invoked that rule since their actions with the hutt weren't as blatantly suicidal or stupid as what I'm suggesting the rule for.</div> </div> </div> </div>A bigger rundown/back story, is that the messing with the hutt like that, was their 6th time and after each prior time, the level of response from the hutt Increased, proportionally.. So since that was an effective attempt to kill him off IN his house (so to speak), the level of response was similar.. As to contacts coming out, and warning them, I see them the way white wolf has it in 2e basic and revised... Where they are someone who does favors for one another, but does not put their life on the line unless they either know the reward for giving the info is worth more, or they owe a big favor...<br /> So with that thinking on how contacts operate, i made the decision that those contacts who DID know of this hutt contract, would tell if approached, but would not make the approach themselves... for fear of peeving off the hutt themselves. Not once did the players check in with ANY of their contacts, while on down time and even with me giving 6 times during that 'down time' to notice tails and suss out someone's following and watching them, none of them made the rolls needed. <br /> Now usually in games, when i ask for those sorts of rolls out of the blue like that, the FACT that they are making those rolls, especially when in a supposed safe zone, normally tweeks the mind that something's amiss.. However not ONE of them seemed to work that fact out..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cynic01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/913570-hints-warnings-and-insta-kill-powers-can-the-latter-be-used-on-pcs?p=913616#post913616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You said you kept track of dice rolls and such for the snipers, but if they basically all succeeded the players had no idea what was going on (and just assuming the ST is up to something because they are rolling dice should not be the only hint as that is purely out of game knowledge). As an outsider looking in here is what I think might have gone through your player's heads, &quot;The ST is pissed we messed up his hutt NPC so he made these godlike snipers to hunt us down, and because he didn't &quot;fail&quot; his rolls [which I'm assuming weren't rolled with the players knowledge] we get shot with no chance to defend ourselves; might have just as well said rocks fall everyone dies.&quot; Basically it looks like you took unilateral revenge against the characters through ST fiat (again assuming rolls weren't made in front if the players)</div> </div> </div> </div>All the backround rolls they made, such as their investigations, searching around and the like, to LEARN the pc's habits, locate them, trail them etc, were done off screen.. Occasionally i even had a player make one or two of those rolls and just tell me the score..<br /> BUT when it came to the actual opposed search-sneak to first see if the party was surprised, the shots, the damage vs soak.. those were all in the open with them making rolls as needed...<br /> I had hot dice, they had real cold ones..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T01:51:31-07:00","id":913957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/913570-hints-warnings-and-insta-kill-powers-can-the-latter-be-used-on-pcs?p=913904#post913904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So even after all sorts of hints, warnings and such were given, just cause it 'squishes fun' don't have it go off, or neuter it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes! The job of the storyteller is to keep the game fun for everyone (yourself included). If a roll or decision causes <b>all</b> of your players to become miserable it is <b>the wrong fucking decision.</b> Bottom line. It doesn't matter that the dice were hot, or that they could theoretically have caught onto the plan, because at the end of it all your players didn't enjoy the experience. <br /> <br /> Now that doesn't mean you have to hold their hands to avoid threatening them, but there are a lot of things you can do to create tension without killing a character. Crippling wounds, getting knocked unconscious or captured, tweaking damage such that it is injuring without being immediately fatal, the many supernatural debuffs and disadvantages that can be levied. Death should be a last resort.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/913570-hints-warnings-and-insta-kill-powers-can-the-latter-be-used-on-pcs?p=913904#post913904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a related q.. Say in game someone has a Maneuver that if used can do X minimum damage, which to a normal &quot;healthy&quot; person would put them CLOSE to death (ie for vampire, it takes them down to the <i>Crippled, -5d</i> level, but the baddie who has that maneuver is in combat with someone who's already down to say <i>wounded, -2d</i> level, so if its USED the minmum damage would kill said pc..<br /> Do you have him use said maneuver? If not, why not??</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd modify the maneuver in the moment to maintain excitement. Probably just put the character to critical, assuming that's what the scene required. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T08:30:40-07:00","id":914106,"title":"","content":"Sounds to me like you are advocating that the DM fudge the dice to avoid killing pcs, since pc death is unfun..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T08:46:56-07:00","id":914113,"title":"","content":"Ok, getting OFF that subject since it seems some are very heated in their ideas on things..<br /> <br /> Here is a few others to ponder...<br /> <br /> Scenario. Players are mixed up in spots on a large vehicle (say they just commandeered a Spectre gunship for a WW game, or are in a Millennium falcon style starship for Star Wars).. ONE of the party is doing the piloting, no one else is near by. BUT he is doing something so stupid that if allowed to finish it off, will cause the ship to blow up causing everyone on it to die (Smash it into a mountain, charge it into an asteroid etc).. Even WITH the dm (and some other players) warning him, he still says &quot;I DO IT!&quot;..<br /> How can the other's survive? Do you just prevent him from doing it anyway??<br /> <br /> Scenario 2. Players have researched a new baddie that cropped up on the &quot;Playing field&quot;, and learned that even though he is a &quot;Might makes right, the weak need to pay&quot; type of dictatorial ruler, he is ALSO honorable/follows his oath(s) given.<br /> In said research, they realize that he is VERY strong and at their 'current level/skill capacity' they are sorely outmatched and SHOULD avoid him till they learn more/gain more.. BUT for what ever dumb reason, they still decide to go against him and soundly get beaten down.. Several are down and out cold, some might even be close to bleeding to death. The 2-3 survivors standing though regain their senses and offer up a surrender. They will pay over XYZ in ransom and swear an oath to stay away from him for ABC time frame.<br /> HE agrees, and starts collecting up said 'ransom'. One of those healed up back to consciousness, decides he doesn't like said deal, but realizes going against the group overtly is dumb, but still tries to get out of it, by either switching out what was promised as part of the ransom, stealing it back once it got piled up, or the like.<br /> AND gets caught!!! Baddie starts wailing on HIM for being dishonorable and renigging on the parlay... A few others step up to defend the dumb one, the others stay out of it...<br /> <br /> Does the baddie, just take it out on HIM and the few others 'stepping up', or all the group??? If taken down again (more than likely a certainty), does he show mercy a 2nd time and let them surrender?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T09:19:06-07:00","id":914132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/913570-hints-warnings-and-insta-kill-powers-can-the-latter-be-used-on-pcs?p=914113#post914113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, getting OFF that subject since it seems some are very heated in their ideas on things..<br /> <br /> Here is a few others to ponder...<br /> <br /> Scenario. Players are mixed up in spots on a large vehicle (say they just commandeered a Spectre gunship for a WW game, or are in a Millennium falcon style starship for Star Wars).. ONE of the party is doing the piloting, no one else is near by. BUT he is doing something so stupid that if allowed to finish it off, will cause the ship to blow up causing everyone on it to die (Smash it into a mountain, charge it into an asteroid etc).. Even WITH the dm (and some other players) warning him, he still says &quot;I DO IT!&quot;..<br /> How can the other's survive? Do you just prevent him from doing it anyway??<br /> <br /> Scenario 2. Players have researched a new baddie that cropped up on the &quot;Playing field&quot;, and learned that even though he is a &quot;Might makes right, the weak need to pay&quot; type of dictatorial ruler, he is ALSO honorable/follows his oath(s) given.<br /> In said research, they realize that he is VERY strong and at their 'current level/skill capacity' they are sorely outmatched and SHOULD avoid him till they learn more/gain more.. BUT for what ever dumb reason, they still decide to go against him and soundly get beaten down.. Several are down and out cold, some might even be close to bleeding to death. The 2-3 survivors standing though regain their senses and offer up a surrender. They will pay over XYZ in ransom and swear an oath to stay away from him for ABC time frame.<br /> HE agrees, and starts collecting up said 'ransom'. One of those healed up back to consciousness, decides he doesn't like said deal, but realizes going against the group overtly is dumb, but still tries to get out of it, by either switching out what was promised as part of the ransom, stealing it back once it got piled up, or the like.<br /> AND gets caught!!! Baddie starts wailing on HIM for being dishonorable and renigging on the parlay... A few others step up to defend the dumb one, the others stay out of it...<br /> <br /> Does the baddie, just take it out on HIM and the few others 'stepping up', or all the group??? If taken down again (more than likely a certainty), does he show mercy a 2nd time and let them surrender?</div> </div> </div> </div>Scenario 1) Either you prevent him from doing it or you only have his character die in the ensuing aftermath. What you can get away with depends on the situation. Assuming it is a technological ship with a computer, there are going to be multiple failsafes to prevent the ship from doing what the player is trying to do, and since they just commandeered it the character probably doesn't know how to get around those and the ship's computer prevents him from doing it. If the ship is older and doesn't/can't have such features, try to figure out a way to save the other characters while letting the fool suffer the fate of the stupid, in a crash the pilot section takes the initial impact whereas the other sections while damaged survive (as to the other players, injured but alive), in the ship blows up scenario you could say that the other characters where thrown clear and the stupid one was not. All that said, if this represents a pattern of the player making these kinds of choices you may have to talk with them out of game, as disruptions like this can ruin the game for everyone else. If it keeps happening even after talking to the player out of game, you may have to tell that player he is no longer welcome at the table.<br /> <br /> Scenario 2) Sounds like the perfect spot for my house rule, make it very clear to all players that tackling this guy is a <b>FATAL </b>idea and that you have already showed immense leniency in giving them a way out of their previous foolishness and that if they throw down you will not pull your punches, their characters die so be it no amount of pleading or sulking will change that, <b>They. Were. Warned. </b>Then ask again very clearly if anyone is going to try fighting the villain now, and if anyone does, go to town and teach the players dumb enough to slap away your kindness the errors of their ways. Then when the dust settles get new sheets and have them make new characters. If the player who got caught decides to change their action the villain can say something like this, &quot;I understand your frustration at the lack of agency and representation you had at the last agreement. Now I am a hard, but fair man so I will give you a choice pay [additional ransom] and swear [oath appropriate] and I will let you walk out of here with your life; same agreement they had the choice to make you now have the conscious choice to make. <b>BUT </b>I will warn you, you cross me again and I will not be so kind, I will strike down upon you as the Lord did upon Sodom and Gomorrah and you will die in a way more horrible than you can imagine.&quot; Then make it clear to the players the next time they go up against this guy there will be no fudged dice and no villainous reprieve, either they are ready or they die, end of story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01","name":"Cynic01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T09:33:34-07:00","id":914144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cynic01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/913570-hints-warnings-and-insta-kill-powers-can-the-latter-be-used-on-pcs?p=914132#post914132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now I am a hard, but fair man so I will give you a choice pay [additional ransom] and swear [oath appropriate] and I will let you walk out of here with your life; same agreement they had the choice to make you now have the conscious choice to make. <b>BUT </b>I will warn you, you cross me again and I will not be so kind, I will strike down upon you as the Lord did upon Sodom and Gomorrah and you will die in a way more horrible than you can imagine.&quot; Then make it clear to the players the next time they go up against this guy there will be no fudged dice and no villainous reprieve, either they are ready or they die, end of story.</div> </div> </div> </div>I almost expected you to quote Jules (Sam Jackson's character in Pulp Fiction) there....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T11:03:31-07:00","id":914218,"title":"","content":"For your scenario 1, really your situation is that one player is trying to kill other players' characters. If that's not clear to everyone, then you need to talk more about the consequences of his choice.<br /> <br /> So strip away the ship and all the rest. Would you let one PC shoot all the other PCs in the head and then himself? If your group's really into PvP and they've been trying to screw each other throughout the game, no problem. This isn't happening because they never thought the PLAYER would betray the group in such a manner, but because that CHARACTER managed to be cleverer than their character. They never had expectations that the group was fundamentally cooperative and so you're not breaking that expectation by allowing this to happen.<br /> <br /> For most games, though, players have that expectation, and allowing one player to basically end the game is unfair to the other players. You can rationalize it however you want in the game, but that doesn't really matter, because you guys aren't really cowboys in the Old West, or wizards in the 11th century, or vampires on the streets of Chicago. You're a group of friends playing a game, and that's more important than the verisimilitude of the game itself.<br /> <br /> I feel like that question of verisimilitude is at the heart of all your questions here. You're unsure about stopping the malicious crashing of the Millennium Falcon because any way you stop it in the game will be unrealistic and &quot;deus ex machina&quot;. You're surprised at the player's objections to the sniper attacks because you feel they are the most realistic thing that would happen in the game world. You don't want to weaken the &quot;cripple maneuver&quot; when it would kill a PC because there's no ingame reason that the bad guy's maneuver would be weaker than normal.<br /> <br /> There's nothing wrong with wanting a realistic game, but you need to set those expectations at the beginning of your game and let folks opt-out then if they want. You might also want to play a game where recovering from death is a possibility, like Eclipse Phase, where dead characters just suffer a monetary penalty for being downloaded into a fresh body.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T11:33:06-07:00","id":914237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/913570-hints-warnings-and-insta-kill-powers-can-the-latter-be-used-on-pcs?p=914106#post914106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds to me like you are advocating that the DM fudge the dice to avoid killing pcs, since pc death is unfun..</div> </div> </div> </div>That's precisely what I'm advocating. Does that really sound so bad?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T12:19:33-07:00","id":914268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/913570-hints-warnings-and-insta-kill-powers-can-the-latter-be-used-on-pcs?p=914237#post914237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's precisely what I'm advocating. Does that really sound so bad?</div> </div> </div> </div>My first ST joked that it was cute how people thought he was accurately reporting <i>any </i>of the rolls he made behind the screen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T12:26:02-07:00","id":914273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/913570-hints-warnings-and-insta-kill-powers-can-the-latter-be-used-on-pcs?p=914268#post914268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My first ST joked that it was cute how people thought he was accurately reporting <i>any </i>of the rolls he made behind the screen.</div> </div> </div> </div>If y'all had fun I'd say he was making the right call. Dice fudging is only bad when the GM is using it to abuse the players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T12:54:44-07:00","id":914290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/913570-hints-warnings-and-insta-kill-powers-can-the-latter-be-used-on-pcs?p=914273#post914273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If y'all had fun I'd say he was making the right call. Dice fudging is only bad when the GM is using it to abuse the players.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I've made the same joke to my players about my ST style, so definitely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T15:37:32-07:00","id":914429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haldir2012</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/913570-hints-warnings-and-insta-kill-powers-can-the-latter-be-used-on-pcs?p=914218#post914218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For your scenario 1, really your situation is that one player is trying to kill other players' characters. If that's not clear to everyone, then you need to talk more about the consequences of his choice.<br /> <br /> So strip away the ship and all the rest. Would you let one PC shoot all the other PCs in the head and then himself? If your group's really into PvP and they've been trying to screw each other throughout the game, no problem. This isn't happening because they never thought the PLAYER would betray the group in such a manner, but because that CHARACTER managed to be cleverer than their character. They never had expectations that the group was fundamentally cooperative and so you're not breaking that expectation by allowing this to happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>In a way it does sound like a case of PVP.. The actual situation i had where the PC was doing something that if it went pear shaped would kill everyone came at a Star wars Convention game, where the pilot of the party's ship decided to head at almost flank speed AT a imperial capital ship (Carrack light cruiser), to get over it and then into it's rear. He felt that cause 'game mechanics wise' ships of higher scale took a Penalty to their die roll to hit the smaller ship (fighter scale here), that combined with the standard 'range base difficulty), they wouldn't have a chance of hitting. So kept refusing to make a DODGE roll (which would have added that scale difference TO), pushing that not a chance to almost a certainty of missing. BUT if hit, the scale diff gets added to the DAMAGE the bigger ship causes when it hits..<br /> Even with ME and 3 of the other players on the table, talking to the player in out of character mode, he still said &quot;Screw it. Just go ahead and roll the ship's to hit, and we will see what happens..&quot;<br /> <br /> So i did. Then i took out a # of D6 for the damage, and then added the 6 more dice in scale, and layed it on the table in front of him, saying &quot;THAT is the amount of damage dice i will now be rolling against you. Since you are all alone in the cockpit and have alreayd locked your ship's shields in the rear arc since that's where the Tie fighters are firing from and have NOT stated you are taking an action to try and re-route them to the front (now grabbing the # of dice for his ship's hull rating which is what the soak roll would be), THIS is what you get to resist it with. Are you SURE that is what you are wanting...&quot; <br /> he said yes again... So i rolled damage, and had him roll the ship's hull. Result, ship blown up twice over... THEN he whines and asks &quot;can i take it back and get a dodge roll now..<br /> As one of the other players on the table was a fellow DM and one of the 'Council members&quot; out group has, he mentioned to that player, &quot;You got plenty of hints, warnings and such.. Now live with it.. though we need to discuss what is gonna happen to everyone ELSE on the bloody ship... DOLT&quot;...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haldir2012</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/913570-hints-warnings-and-insta-kill-powers-can-the-latter-be-used-on-pcs?p=914218#post914218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I feel like that question of verisimilitude is at the heart of all your questions here. You're unsure about stopping the malicious crashing of the Millennium Falcon because any way you stop it in the game will be unrealistic and &quot;deus ex machina&quot;. You're surprised at the player's objections to the sniper attacks because you feel they are the most realistic thing that would happen in the game world. You don't want to weaken the &quot;cripple maneuver&quot; when it would kill a PC because there's no ingame reason that the bad guy's maneuver would be weaker than normal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some of it is that, other aspects is trying to see how other DM's would handle that sort of situation/similar ones..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/913570-hints-warnings-and-insta-kill-powers-can-the-latter-be-used-on-pcs?p=914237#post914237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's precisely what I'm advocating. Does that really sound so bad?</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, Yes pen.. If you are going to roll the dice for something in a GAME, don't ignore it just cause its bad for the players.. Come up with the creative ways to do stuff BEFORE you get to the rolling. <br /> Otherwise, its not a game, and more of 'sitting around a camp fire and telling a story'.. to me. <br /> Plus if i succeed at something, i would RATHER that success come from my own effort (and my team mates) than cause the DM handed us the victory..<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T16:51:04-07:00","id":914463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/913570-hints-warnings-and-insta-kill-powers-can-the-latter-be-used-on-pcs?p=914429#post914429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, Yes pen.. If you are going to roll the dice for something in a GAME, don't ignore it just cause its bad for the players.. Come up with the creative ways to do stuff BEFORE you get to the rolling.<br /> Otherwise, its not a game, and more of 'sitting around a camp fire and telling a story'.. to me.<br /> Plus if i succeed at something, i would RATHER that success come from my own effort (and my team mates) than cause the DM handed us the victory..</div> </div> </div> </div>See, I'd argue that storytelling comes first, and dice are always subservient to the tale, but eh, different strokes for different folks. <br /> <br /> Though, I must make the point that fudging dice is not equivalent to handing a player victory. Indeed, I find I most often fudge rolls when they would otherwise shut down or shit on a player's creative solution. To me dice have nothing to do with effort (unless that effort was to build up as many dice as possible), they are a random element largely out of the players control.<br /> <br /> Again though, different strokes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T17:43:54-07:00","id":914486,"title":"","content":"The guy at the con game sounds like an idiot and I agree you gave him fair warning. But did you do the same for the sniper example? &quot;Hey guys, your characters really pissed off the Hutt there. He's definitely going to have you killed, and he's certainly not going to send Greedo. Are you prepared for that?&quot;<br /> <br /> Let's say they continued to ignore the threat and got sniped. I'd still be willing to retcon that if there's some system misunderstanding at play (&quot;I thought my Danger Sense ability would tell me if anyone pointed a gun at me, no matter how far!&quot;).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T17:44:37-07:00","id":914487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/913570-hints-warnings-and-insta-kill-powers-can-the-latter-be-used-on-pcs?p=914463#post914463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, I'd argue that storytelling comes first, and dice are always subservient to the tale, but eh, different strokes for different folks.<br /> <br /> Though, I must make the point that fudging dice is not equivalent to handing a player victory. Indeed, I find I most often fudge rolls when they would otherwise shut down or shit on a player's creative solution. To me dice have nothing to do with effort (unless that effort was to build up as many dice as possible), they are a random element largely out of the players control.<br /> <br /> Again though, different strokes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thing is, from most every site i have been on, those who often espouse the &quot;Fudge dice&quot; mantra, are ONLY on about fudging dice to HELP the party, whether to stave off death, TPK, Capture etc. Rarely if ever to make things Harder when stuffs going easy for them..<br /> <br /> <br /> Now onto a different Scenario. This came from one of my other gaming sites for ADND, but the poster was more on about a Shadow run game he was a player in..<br /> Dm had it set where the 5 players each with one PC and one controlling a NPC, went up against a larger (10) man force of enemy but they were of lower skill level.. The DM had some House rules on people taking too much damage before dying potentially going out cold (knocked out but could come too later)..<br /> During the battle, it got to where 4 of the baddies were ko'ed, 2 dead, and one severely wounded. BUT 3 of the pcs and the NPC were also down and unconscious.<br /> PC troll decides he's gonna toss a big bomb pack (iirc 6 grenades taped together) to take out the building's south wall, and TRY to take out 2 of the remaining enemy at the same time, and informed the DM his 'booma pack' was set for 3 second detonation after it HITS something. Rolls his to hit, and gets a Critical botch (iirc it was described as 6 of the 9 dice he rolled were 1s and not ONE of the 3 remaining were successes, meaning 5 or more), so effectively dropped it at his FEET (it was a common HR the group had been using for a while now..<br /> He decides to drop ON the grenade pack, thinking &quot;I am a tough b/stard, and can spend Karma to soak it all, when the other PC's pointed out, while HE might survive, the koed ones lying around him wouldn't.<br /> DM gave him the option &quot;Take it all and have a redmist effect (IE you die) but everyone else's saved, or spend karma to soak it, but they also take damage.. He spent almost half an hour trying to argue with the DM, feeling that by MECHANICs alone he should have been able to take the ENTIRE blow himself with no affecting anyone else..<br /> <br /> What say you all there??<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T19:26:50-07:00","id":914576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/913570-hints-warnings-and-insta-kill-powers-can-the-latter-be-used-on-pcs?p=914487#post914487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thing is, from most every site i have been on, those who often espouse the &amp;quot;Fudge dice&amp;quot; mantra, are ONLY on about fudging dice to HELP the party, whether to stave off death, TPK, Capture etc. Rarely if ever to make things Harder when stuffs going easy for them..<br /> <br /> <br /> Now onto a different Scenario. This came from one of my other gaming sites for ADND, but the poster was more on about a Shadow run game he was a player in..<br /> Dm had it set where the 5 players each with one PC and one controlling a NPC, went up against a larger (10) man force of enemy but they were of lower skill level.. The DM had some House rules on people taking too much damage before dying potentially going out cold (knocked out but could come too later)..<br /> During the battle, it got to where 4 of the baddies were ko'ed, 2 dead, and one severely wounded. BUT 3 of the pcs and the NPC were also down and unconscious.<br /> PC troll decides he's gonna toss a big bomb pack (iirc 6 grenades taped together) to take out the building's south wall, and TRY to take out 2 of the remaining enemy at the same time, and informed the DM his 'booma pack' was set for 3 second detonation after it HITS something. Rolls his to hit, and gets a Critical botch (iirc it was described as 6 of the 9 dice he rolled were 1s and not ONE of the 3 remaining were successes, meaning 5 or more), so effectively dropped it at his FEET (it was a common HR the group had been using for a while now..<br /> He decides to drop ON the grenade pack, thinking &amp;quot;I am a tough b/stard, and can spend Karma to soak it all, when the other PC's pointed out, while HE might survive, the koed ones lying around him wouldn't.<br /> DM gave him the option &amp;quot;Take it all and have a redmist effect (IE you die) but everyone else's saved, or spend karma to soak it, but they also take damage.. He spent almost half an hour trying to argue with the DM, feeling that by MECHANICs alone he should have been able to take the ENTIRE blow himself with no affecting anyone else..<br /> <br /> What say you all there??</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not let him? Jumping on grenades and surviving is actually a REAL world event. They get usually give the living and the dead the highest medal in the military services for it. And people survive it. Just like when a parachute fails to open and they plunge 10000 feet to their...... Broken ankle?!!!! Yup people are both tougher and more fragile than game mechanics are. The Storyteller has to be on the side of the players, because otherwise is the Universe is definitely against them. Crits and fumbles hurt player more than The GM. Why? The GM rolls for the ENTIRE UNIVERSE!!!! As storyteller, I CONTROL EVERYTHING not directly attacked to a player. EVERYONE and Everything. The players got exactly what's written on there Character sheets and WHAT I GIVE. So your not fugding the dice to unfairly help then. Your giving them a little Plot immunity, because they are the most important thing in the game. Not the most powerful, or influential( unless they RPed to get there), but definitely the most important. PCs are the protagonist in your group. So they can be the cast from Star Wars or Star Trek. Or they are the cast from Game of Thrones. But tell them which world they are in before hand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11217-kurseteller","name":"kurseteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T04:49:24-07:00","id":914748,"title":"","content":"If you make a threat, there has to be consequences. As we can see there are two components to this sentence a.) the threat and b.) the consequence. <br /> <br /> You should never make a threat to kill a character - even if it is as subtle as a dice roll for perception+alertness in a tense situation - if you would not go through with it. If the prince says, if you betray me you will die, that should happen or the prince will look weak. That itself can be a great plot point, if it fits his/her character, but a competent prince won't say that in the first place if a PC is not as disposable as he/she seems to be. Which is why most important people should make vague, veiled threats. <br /> <br /> I kill off PCs from time to time, but that is because every PC involved lives a dangerous life. I would destroy a huge part of my Group if there were none. Trust in the ST also means to trust that while he will not kill a PC off for no reason, he will do it if there are enough. There is not much worse than the over protective ST that sacrifices a good scene of RP, plot and story because he is not able to stand up to their players in regards to character death. If you walk into the metaphorical lion den, while screaming that you do not want to be rescued or captured together with the fact that the PC is not backing down what so ever... well you die.<br /> <br /> Someone said, that there has to be a trust between the ST and the PCs which is absolutely right and in the way the sniper killed them can be seen as that. Note, that PenDragon wrote in the TL<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />R that those forces were unforeseen, which is something i actually agree with. If there were enough hints and the ST has to make the decision to kill of a PC we have a different situation.<br /> <br /> First of all not ALL people in the group will be happy to see a character live if he did things that would kill him normally. I would go so far and say that if the ST itself gets miserable by killing (or letting him survive) of a PC for no other reason then relationships to your player you might want to think about that first. Personally i think that it can happen but not too often. Maybe it is time to get back and play yourself again. The PCs will feel that weakness instinctively and might even subconsciously take advantage of it.<br /> The second case is if people are just dense and are not getting hints. Sometimes people talk of bred crumbs, but more often than not you should throw the whole bakery in their face. Give people a death vision, a let them make self control roles to stay where they are or instinct role and give them chills. <br /> Third point is an easy one - communicate with your players more and not only before or after the game. Tell them how close they were to death if they were in a difficult situation. It works wonders when you tell people just how lucky they are.<br /> <br /> That said it is way more effective to maim their favorite pet ghouls, let them be betrayed by their significant others or let their mentors, allies and contacts die off one by one. Some of my best scenes happened with these kind of things and while a death scene can be immensely rewarding the feel of a loss on their character sheets seem to be strong enough for people. <br /> <br /> Case in point, a PC of mine went after a Nosferatu who disrupted the party of his mentor by kidnapping the lead singer. The Nosferatu was quite a bit ahead, but the PC had a cat ghoul with a fine nose. Everyone loved that cat, its personality was your typical cat personality. Self important, arrogant but oh so cute. The Nosferatu went into a forest and they followed him. The situation got tenser and tenser as they came closer to the territory of a Gangrel who's relationship with the Carmarilla was strained at best. The cat and the PC got separated because the cat had less problems with the terrain. After more and more howls of wolfs they the PC found his Ghoul stiff as a brick in the middle of a glade. When he walke up to her to look if she was still alive he realizes that he is surrounded by 10 wolfs all in attack mode. <br /> <br /> He gets out of it and he is able to rescue his cat, but that cat had a full slate of agg. Damage and he literally fed her the necessary blood night for night until she was okay again. She died shortly after through a Sabbat attack though. <br /> <br /> And the Moral of the story is - don't attack the PC, attack the things or individuals he or she loves most.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash","name":"Crytash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T13:30:46-07:00","id":918778,"title":"","content":"My general mantra in the World of Darkness is &quot;If you kill the PC, the torment ends&quot;. If the dice say someone should die, and that's not fun for the player, it doesn't kill them, because that's just a sudden end to the story, and isn't very interesting for anyone. Instead, you apply a flaw, long term damage, or something plot-heavy that will spur roleplaying opportunities and continue the story, while still making it clear the character &quot;lost&quot; in that instance. If a mental assault would kill someone, gve them some nightmarish flaw and/or derangement, if they'd be torn up by claws, give them a deformity or take away an appendage, and similar, and then make sure it's something they need to go through some plot to fix, one way or another.<br /> <br /> That said, I do agree with the 'Are you sure?' sort of rule when someone's going to do something that really just IS blatantly stupid, because otherwise the game starts getting silly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T10:38:38-07:00","id":920451,"title":"","content":"IMO players shouldn't be immune to the consequences of their in game actions. It sounds to me like the players were showboating and causing trouble without regard to the possibility that death can even happen to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2818-frostfox","name":"FrostFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T13:41:20-07:00","id":920536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FrostFox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/913570-hints-warnings-and-insta-kill-powers-can-the-latter-be-used-on-pcs?p=920451#post920451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IMO players shouldn't be immune to the consequences of their in game actions. It sounds to me like the players were showboating and causing trouble without regard to the possibility that death can even happen to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, from speaking with 2 of those players IN that OP issue, a few weeks later after everyone had calmed down, they were more peeved i actually went through with it, cause they had played under other DMs who DIDN'T make pcs liable to face consequences of their actions.. So it was more that they were used to not facing the effects of what they caused coming back to bite them in the butts, more so than showboating..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T16:58:52-07:00","id":920631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/913570-hints-warnings-and-insta-kill-powers-can-the-latter-be-used-on-pcs?p=920536#post920536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, from speaking with 2 of those players IN that OP issue, a few weeks later after everyone had calmed down, they were more peeved i actually went through with it, cause they had played under other DMs who DIDN'T make pcs liable to face consequences of their actions.. So it was more that they were used to not facing the effects of what they caused coming back to bite them in the butts, more so than showboating..</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah but thinking there's no real consequences leads to showboating and not really obeying the spirit of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2818-frostfox","name":"FrostFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T23:42:49-07:00","id":920845,"title":"","content":"True dat.. <br /> <br /> <br /> OK. Another situation to ponder.. (again from a SW game)..<br /> <br /> By the rules, if you get knocked out (Via stun damage, you are out cold for 2d minutes. If you get incapacitated by lethal (no stun) damage its lights out for 10d minutes.<br /> Where as if you are mortally wounded, you roll 2d, and if the # is LESS than the # of rounds you have been at MW, you pass away.<br /> Combat situation has 6 pcs fighting one powerful baddie, but in a manner where he 'gauges' their combat skills, and if very low he doesn't even bother with them, thinking them not worthy of fighting (Up till they actually hit him that is). Equal skill level are toyed with, while those of 'higher' level, are 'threats to get taken out with extreme prejudice..<br /> <br /> During the fight, 3 of the pcs go down to incap. 3 others drop to mortally wounded. Baddie leaves.<br /> <br /> Since no one else is around, how can you NOT have those 3 at mortally wounded die??","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T07:47:37-07:00","id":927053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/913570-hints-warnings-and-insta-kill-powers-can-the-latter-be-used-on-pcs?p=920845#post920845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True dat.. <br /> <br /> <br /> OK. Another situation to ponder.. (again from a SW game)..<br /> <br /> By the rules, if you get knocked out (Via stun damage, you are out cold for 2d minutes. If you get incapacitated by lethal (no stun) damage its lights out for 10d minutes.<br /> Where as if you are mortally wounded, you roll 2d, and if the # is LESS than the # of rounds you have been at MW, you pass away.<br /> Combat situation has 6 pcs fighting one powerful baddie, but in a manner where he 'gauges' their combat skills, and if very low he doesn't even bother with them, thinking them not worthy of fighting (Up till they actually hit him that is). Equal skill level are toyed with, while those of 'higher' level, are 'threats to get taken out with extreme prejudice..<br /> <br /> During the fight, 3 of the pcs go down to incap. 3 others drop to mortally wounded. Baddie leaves.<br /> <br /> Since no one else is around, how can you NOT have those 3 at mortally wounded die??</div> </div> </div> </div>Simple:<br /> The Baddie wants them to suffer more and takes them into slavery. Next story is to escape without their beloved stuff.<br /> Or take another baddie(a weaker one taking advantage of the situation)<br /> Or another npc that expects they pay him back this boon.<br /> <br /> Or, as mentioned before, take the rule that they die Within x turns with a grain of salt and let them survive but with a flaw(ugly scars, short of breath, missing limbs etc.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T14:25:41-07:00","id":927281,"title":"","content":"For me it's all about the magic word: Agency. Do your players have Agency? Consult the following list:<br /> <br /> - Are your players in control of the actions of their characters?<br /> - Are your players able to interact with the world within the scope of said world, the abilities of their characters and the social contract of the group?<br /> - Are your players aware of what the consequences of their actions might be?<br /> <br /> The first one is pretty simple. Can your players decide what to do with their characters? Or are they limited in some way?<br /> The second can be answered by considering if you'd say &quot;no&quot; to a player's desire to perform a certain action. If you do this a lot you might very well be railroading. This one is a tricky one, because players that stay within the boundaries might very well derail your campaign, even unintentionally.<br /> The third is having a reasonable cause and effect. For example, a Toreador is going to a bar to pick someone up for a meal. Having the player roll as normal and succeed at getting their fill is acceptable. Having the target suddenly and straight out of nowhere appear to be bait set by a group of Hunters to ambush the Toreador is bad sport. Actually foreshadowing that there are Hunters on the prowl before the Toreador goes out for a drink, or draw extra attention to this particular person is acceptable, because it hints at the fact that something might be off.<br /> <br /> So, are the above three questions all answered with yes? Then congratulations, your players have Agency! This means that all the bad things that happen to them happened for a reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}